module gunbc.typed_module_cache_capacity


// WHY THIS MODULE EXISTS. extdeps.realization.reconcile_in_process declares the
// typed module cache's ceiling as RuntimeDerivedLimit { authority: ... }, and
// that authority pointed at v1_compiler.cli_run typed_module_cache_cap_derivation
// -- a hand-Rust symbol spelled inside a DeclarationRef. A DeclarationRef is
// structurally a reference to a MODULED declaration, so putting a seed symbol in
// one makes an unmodelled fact look resolved: nothing in the corpus states the
// division, the clamp, or the refusal, and no reader can check the seed against
// anything. RuntimeDerivedLimit is honest that the VALUE is computed at run
// start; it is not licence for the DERIVATION to be unmodelled.
//
// So the derivation lands here as the authority, and the seed keeps its own copy
// as a declared Scaffold below rather than as an implicit fork.
data typed_module_cache_capacity_note: String = "The typed-module-cache entry cap, modelled. The cap bounds the memory used to RESOLVE the corpus, which is why the seed cannot simply read this value: cli_run enforce_typed_cache_entry_cap needs it while modules are being resolved, so it cannot be a value obtained by resolving them. That is a genuine bootstrap constraint rather than ordinary seed-shrink debt, and it is the reason the mirror below is a Scaffold with a stated dissolution rather than a deletion. What changes here is which side is the AUTHORITY: this module states the derivation, and the seed is checkable against it.\n\nThe three constants are cited to the v1-run-stability M0/M1 receipts (~2-11 MiB per module observed; 3 MiB is the interim declared denominator until measured space lands) and the floor/ceiling the seed already enforces. The refusal arm is not a default: an unreadable budget yields CapEntryRefused, never the ceiling. That distinction is the whole receipt of gunbc.host_budget_source no_fallback_arm_note -- the previous unwrap_or(CEIL) turned an unknown budget into the most permissive cap available and OOM-killed the witness corpus twice."

data typed_module_bytes_per_entry_estimate: std.measure.ByteSize = byte_size(count: 3145728)

data typed_module_cache_entries_floor: Int = 100

data typed_module_cache_entries_ceiling: Int = 4000

// Two states, because "derived a bound" and "could not" have different remedies
// and only the first may bound a resolve. There is deliberately no arm carrying
// a fallback number.
type TypedModuleCacheCap
  = CapEntries { entries: Int }
  | CapEntryRefused { reason: std.types.NonEmptyStr }

// The derivation the seed hand-realizes. Division by the per-entry estimate,
// then clamped into the declared band -- the clamp is what keeps a very small
// budget from producing a cap of zero (which would thrash) and a very large one
// from producing an unbounded working set.
fn typed_module_cache_entry_cap(r: gunbc.host_budget_source.HostBudgetResolution) -> TypedModuleCacheCap {
  match r {
    HostBudgetResolved { source: _, bytes: b } =>
      CapEntries { entries: clamp_to_declared_band(raw: raw_entry_cap(budget: b)) }
    HostBudgetUnreadable { reason: why } => CapEntryRefused { reason: why }
  }
}

fn raw_entry_cap(budget: std.measure.ByteSize) -> Int {
  byte_size_count(b: budget) / byte_size_count(b: typed_module_bytes_per_entry_estimate)
}

fn clamp_to_declared_band(raw: Int) -> Int {
  int_min(
    a: std.realization_width.int_max(a: raw, b: typed_module_cache_entries_floor),
    b: typed_module_cache_entries_ceiling
  )
}

// The operator/test probe the seed honours: a positive override is accepted but
// still clamped to the ceiling, so the probe can never widen past the modelled
// band. A zero or negative override is not an override at all -- it falls
// through to the derived cap rather than being treated as "no limit".
fn typed_module_cache_entry_cap_with_override(
  override_entries: Int,
  r: gunbc.host_budget_source.HostBudgetResolution
) -> TypedModuleCacheCap {
  if override_entries > 0 {
    CapEntries { entries: int_min(a: override_entries, b: typed_module_cache_entries_ceiling) }
  } else {
    typed_module_cache_entry_cap(r: r)
  }
}

fn typed_module_cache_cap_is_refused(c: TypedModuleCacheCap) -> Bool {
  match c {
    CapEntries { entries: _ } => false
    CapEntryRefused { reason: _ } => true
  }
}

data typed_module_cache_capacity_seed_mirror_disposition: std.disposition.Disposition = std.disposition.Scaffold {
  dissolves_to: SingleAuthority,
  bind: std.decl_ref.DeclarationRef {
    module_path: "gunbc.typed_module_cache_capacity",
    decl_name: "typed_module_cache_entry_cap",
    field: WholeDeclaration
  }
}

data typed_module_cache_capacity_seed_mirror_note: String = "v1_compiler.cli_run typed_module_cache_cap_derivation IS THIS DERIVATION, hand-realized in the seed, and it is declared here rather than left implicit. It composes the same division, the same floor/ceiling clamp, the same positive-override rule, and the same refusal -- and nothing executes a check that the two agree, which is exactly the drift this repository has already paid for elsewhere.\n\nWhy it cannot be deleted today: the cap bounds the memory used to RESOLVE the corpus, so its consumer runs strictly before any .dag value could exist. The seed needs the value baked in. That is a bootstrap constraint, not ordinary seed-shrink debt, and conflating the two would misprice the work.\n\nTHE INTERIM LENS NOW EXISTS AND EXECUTES: test.claim.seed_mirror_constant_lens_witness_test joins all five in-scope seed constants to their authority rows, including this module's three. It derives each expected literal from the row rather than writing it down, so it cannot be satisfied by editing the lens, and it REFUSES an uncited or unparseable constant rather than skipping it. This paragraph previously described that lens in the future tense while nothing executed, and a dissolution trigger naming a mechanism that does not run reads as guarded to every later author -- which is measured, not hypothetical: DECLARED_RUNNER_SLOT_MEMORY_HIGH_BYTES sat eleven days at a value its authority had superseded, under exactly this sentence.

WHAT REMAINS UNDISSOLVED, which is the larger half: the lens checks that the mirror AGREES, not that the mirror is unnecessary. The full dissolution is still the emit path baking this module's constants into the seed so cli_run stops composing its own arithmetic and reads them. Until that lands the AGREEMENT half of this class remains MITIGATABLE, and the 2026-08-20 correction below is to the REASON rather than to the rung.\n\nWHAT THIS SENTENCE SAID AND WHY IT CHANGED: it read that the lens declares ReadsLiveTree because it reads .rs text, that the required floor folds one hermetic subject, and that the lens is therefore DISCOVERED AND DECLINED with nothing executing it automatically. The measurement in it is preserved and still correct -- adding the lens moved the floor's declined_live count by exactly its four witnesses and its claims count by zero (gunbc#8638, run 32337765205 against 32333231183 at the same base). The INFERENCE from it was wrong. A hermetic Filesystem.Read of a committed checkout path is input access rather than a host effect (v1_interpreter's checkout-read carve-out), so reading committed .rs text never actually required a non-hermetic route; what declines the lens is a separate file-grain prediction in the floor's site projection, which is measured as removable (floor run 32345970386: deleted on a branch, ~783 identities admitted, 626 pass) but is NOT yet removed on main, because the same deletion admits 55 blockers staged behind their own owners. So the rung stays where it was and the path to climbing it is now known and cheap rather than unknown.\n\nTHE UNDISSOLVED HALF IS UNCHANGED AND IS STILL THE LARGER ONE: the lens checks that the mirror AGREES, not that the mirror is unnecessary, and the full dissolution remains the emit path baking this module's constants into the seed so cli_run stops composing its own arithmetic and reads them. test.claim.seed_mirror_constant_lens_witness_test seed_mirror_lens_floor_execution_note carries the measurement, the correction, and the surviving residual (an unmarked seed constant is invisible to both arms)."
